hi there steve coffin here today i want  to talk about  easy language learning now if you enjoy  these  uh videos about language learning please  subscribe to my channel  language learning is not easy it's not  easy because we have to force our brain  to become accustomed to a new way of  saying things new sounds new structures  new  ways that words are put together  this is not easy it's actually a  quite a complex process i believe having  gone through it many times where we  transform ourselves into  natural speakers of another language so  the whole process is not easy  however the things that we do  to help us get there we can choose to do  things that are inherently difficult  demanding stressful or we can choose to  do things that are easy  i prefer to do things that are easy  for example i find listening and reading  more enjoyable and therefore easier than  doing drills and exercises  i find that doing translation  is difficult whereas just allowing the  language to come into you is easier  when i do flashcards or  any of the activities that we have at  link which include closed tests and  multiple choice i want them to be easy  i'm just kind of flipping through these  words it's another  form of exposure to these new words i  don't want to be racking my brain trying  to think what does this  word mean  uh  you know when i when i uh for example  the  living language book that i occasionally  go to you know they'll introduce um  colors or  numbers  or um  you know names of members of your family  or verb endings and then they  immediately want to test you on it i  don't do these tests because i don't  find that easy  in fact it's very difficult to remember  something that you've just read on or  read about in the chapter it's going to  take a lot more exposure before you can  remember any of this so i don't want to  be tested on it what i find  easy for example is  using my ipad  and reading the variety of beginner  material that we have at link for  example  where i can  you know  basically simply touch words  and hear them pronounced or i can touch  phrases  and so as i'm reading through either  material that i've read before  or new stories that i haven't read and  as i save new words  and create new phrases and highlight  them or look at words and phrases that  were saved before i always get to hear  them and so it's actually a  spectacularly  easy way of plowing through  new texts  and yet listening to bits and pieces as  you read through i find that easy  uh  what else i tried to i was gonna in fact  i will be doing  an in-depth  review of duolingo so i thought i'd give  it a try i went on  in greek  and very quickly they asked you to  translate from english to greek so i've  got to  set up a keyboard and write in greek  which i don't want to do so i'm out of  there  then i thought well i'll do it with an  easier language that i haven't learned  before like dutch where i can at least  type in the uh  you know roman alphabet but even there  it's it's not something that i want to  be doing it's not easy for me i prefer  doing easy things exposure  as i say when i flash card i want all  the results on the front  i don't rack my brain  and so so this is kind of and i've  always felt this way about language  learning when i wrote my book 10 years  ago i had this  taoist  parable about the tree doing things that  are natural doing things that are easy  effortless following your nature  following your interest  that was a symbol that was the  first sort of introduction that i used  and i very much believe this and if we  are able  to uh oh another thing that i find easy  is  varying the content so rather than  forcing yourself to stay on on one  course chapter one two three i find that  by chapter three i'm bored with this and  i prefer to go and do another chapter  one two three of easy material and that  all so i'm exploring it and helped by  the text to speech and all of that is  easy and enjoyable  and i find gets you there  as quickly or more quickly than the sort  of forced  learning that's a part of traditional  instruction so there you have it  language learning isn't easy  but  we can choose to do things that are  enjoyable and easy and not place  unnecessary strain on ourselves and i  think that keeps us going with the  language and that we learn it  naturally and  in my opinion more effectively that way  than in a more stressful and less easy  way so i look forward to hearing your  comments  [Music]  you
 

